# Synchronized Video Context: Visual Anchoring

This plan enhances the [CompacterExtractor](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/lectvideoanalyser/src/extractors/compacter.py#13-180) with a mode that anchors transcript segments to their corresponding visual slides, creating a unified context that is easier for AI to digest without confusion.

## Proposed Changes

### [extractors] [compacter.py](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/lectvideoanalyser/src/extractors/compacter.py)

#### [MODIFY] [compacter.py](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/lectvideoanalyser/src/extractors/compacter.py)
- Update `CompacterExtractor.extract` to support a `visual_anchoring` mode.
- Change the extraction loop to:
  1. Identify "Visual Landmarks" (major slide changes) via OCR/Scene detection.
  2. Map every transcript segment to the *most relevant* visual landmark.
  3. Structure the output as:
     ```markdown
     ## [SLIDE: <Title/OCR Snippet>]
     - [0:00-1:20] Transcript talking about this specific slide.
     - [1:20-2:15] Further explanation of the same slide.
     ```
- Enhance [_is_visual_delta](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/lectvideoanalyser/src/extractors/compacter.py#150-159) to be more robust in identifying slide transitions.

### [services] [output_formatter.py](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/lectvideoanalyser/src/services/output_formatter.py)

#### [MODIFY] [output_formatter.py](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/lectvideoanalyser/src/services/output_formatter.py)
- Update [format_markdown](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/lectvideoanalyser/src/services/output_formatter.py#29-95) to support the "Anchored" structure if the extractor provides it.

## Verification Plan

### Automated Tests
- Test the "mapping" logic: ensure transcript segments from 1:00-2:00 are correctly assigned to the slide identified at 0:55.
- Verify the output string contains the new anchored headers.

### Manual Verification
1. Run a test extraction on a video with clear slide changes.
2. Verify that the transcript flows naturally under the correct slide headers.
